    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d548">

                <pb facs="0496" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg380"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/92.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister to Haiti</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 15, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In regard to your December 2<anchor n="2" xml:id="d548-f1"/>, January 8<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d548-f2"/>, and No. 993 of December 23,<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d548-f3"/> the Department is gratified to know that the Haitian
                    Government has taken vigorous measures against the Dominican revolutionists, and
                    that it is willing to broaden the powers of the boundary plenipotentiary.
                    Similar action is being urged at Santo Domingo by our Legation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d548-f1" n="2" xml:id="d548-f1-content">
                <p>Should he December 22; see <ref target="frus1911#pg_166">For. Rel. 1911, p.
